Independent real-WASM integration probe:
The script below uses the repository's conformance fixture to register test-only successor rule modules. It replaces the actual v1b WASM i32.const -7 instruction, uses the real metered runner and gate, and admits an equivalent rotation followed by an ordinary commit. It does not stub metered results. The E-9 successor declares only {-7}, so its admitted code is not a resource code under the host's own classification. The E-10 positive control declares {-10} and is admitted as well. This demonstrates the generic admission behavior for test-registered successors, not the activation of a new production rules module or a v2 hardening on a live chain. One preliminary probe asserted the governing rules immediately at the rotation tip; the corrected probe below adds the following commit, matching the conformance fixture's observation point.

Run from the checkout using Python with sigma-glyph==0.8.0 installed and node on PATH. Set TMPDIR to a writable scratch directory. The script and its output follow.

```python
import sys
from pathlib import Path
sys.path.insert(0, str(Path.cwd()))
import vars1 as V
from test_vars1 import TestVars1Conformance

t = TestVars1Conformance()
t.setUp()
try:
    inp = t._fuzz_counterexample()
    c1, s0 = t._core()
    prior, s1, _ = t._change('hardening', 'core', c1, s0, V.H_LENS_KERNEL_V1B, label='v1b', inp=inp)
    t.repo.admit_and_advance('core', prior, expected_old=c1)
    assert V.KERNEL1B_ATOM.count(b'\x41\x79') == 1
    for code, declared in [(-9, {-7}), (-10, {-10})]:
        raw = V.KERNEL1B_ATOM.replace(b'\x41\x79', bytes([0x41, code & 0x7f]))
        path = Path(t.tmp.name) / f'successor-{abs(code)}.wasm'
        path.write_bytes(raw)
        h = V.sha256(raw)
        t._register_rules(h, V.Rules(path, 'v1', frozenset(declared)), raw)
        got = V.metered_runner(h).run(inp, t.BUDGET)
        assert got == V.RulesResult('refusal', code=code), got
        next_tip, next_scope, _ = t._change('equivalent', 'core', prior, s1, h, label=f'next-{abs(code)}')
        t.repo.admit_and_advance('core', next_tip, expected_old=prior)
        atoms = {}
        next_tip = t._commit('core', next_tip, next_scope, atoms, [t._axiom(atoms, f'core/after-{abs(code)}', 'after successor')])
        assert t.repo.lens('core')['rules'] == h
        print(f'ADMITTED actual WASM successor: code={got.code}, resource_codes={sorted(declared)}, resource={got.code in declared}, budget={t.BUDGET}', flush=True)
        prior, s1 = next_tip, next_scope
finally:
    t.doCleanups()
    t.tearDown()
    for runner in list(V._KERNELS.values()) + list(V._METERED.values()):
        runner.proc.stdin.close()
        runner.proc.stdout.close()
        runner.proc.wait(timeout=10)

```

